    //Why Agora
    "s1.why": "Data strategy engagements require more than frameworks and slide decks. They require the ability to assess where an organisation genuinely stands, navigate the constraints that make change difficult, and sequence a transformation that is executable under real operational conditions. As a DAMA Certified Data Management Professional with end-to-end experience designing and deploying BCBS239-aligned frameworks, from initial assessment through to full organisational rollout, this service is delivered with the technical depth and executive fluency that complex data transformations demand.",
    "s2.why": "Data Governance frameworks are only as good as their adoption. Designing the right structure is one challenge. Getting an organisation to operate through it is another. Both require having worked at every layer of the model, from defining ownership structures and governance forums with executive teams, to deploying data catalogues and business glossaries on enterprise platforms such as Collibra, to running maturity workshops with business domains to ensure the model is understood and exercised in practice. That end-to-end experience, accumulated across complex regulated environments, is what this service brings to every engagement.",
    "s3.why": "Data quality is the foundation that determines whether an organisation's data can be trusted, exploited and relied upon for critical decisions and regulatory obligations. Building that foundation requires working simultaneously at the technical layer, defining controls, validation rules and monitoring mechanisms, and at the organisational layer, ensuring ownership is active, escalation paths are respected and resolution is traceable. This service has been delivered across complex regulated environments, from designing Critical Data Element frameworks and quality control architectures to coordinating cross-functional remediation programmes between business and technology teams, including data quality strategy design for one of the largest banking migration programmes in recent Spanish history.",
    "s4.why": "Exploiting data effectively requires more than technical capability. It requires understanding what decisions need to be supported, what the analytical infrastructure can realistically sustain and what governance the chosen approach demands. This service draws on direct experience designing executive reporting frameworks and dashboard architectures for senior leadership in tier-one financial institutions, coordinating their implementation with technical teams to ensure consistency and reliability at every layer. On the AI side, the experience goes beyond theory: developing AI service offerings, designing use case evaluation frameworks and conducting ROI assessments that determine whether an AI initiative is worth pursuing before any resource commitment is made. That combination of analytical grounding and disciplined AI evaluation, reinforced by active specialisation in EU AI Act and NIST AI RMF compliance, is what this service brings to every engagement.",
    "s5.why": "Data transformation programmes are won or lost at the human layer. Strategic roadmaps, governance models and data management frameworks only deliver value when the people who need to use them actually do. The experience behind this service comes from having been inside the organisation during that transition, embedded within data domains, working alongside teams as they navigate new ways of working, understanding firsthand where resistance emerges and what it takes to move through it.",

    //Data Strategy & Value Maximization
    "s1.headline": "Data Strategy & Value Maximization",
    "s1.sub1": "Every data transformation starts with a question: where does data stand in the organisation's strategic agenda, and what will it take to unlock its full potential. This service provides that answer through a rigorous assessment of the organisation's data reality, ambitions and constraints, translated into a strategic vision and a prioritised set of actions that reflect both internal objectives and the broader competitive and regulatory landscape.",
    //"s1.sub2": "Data is treated as a strategic asset whose value depends on alignment with organisational objectives and executive intent. Strategic roadmaps are therefore subject to continuous tracking and milestone monitoring, ensuring that initial ambition translates into sustained execution without dilution or drift."
    "s1.pillar1": "Definition of an enterprise data vision aligned with corporate strategy, executive priorities and the external landscape, including regulatory constraints, competitive dynamics and sector-specific data requirements.",
    "s1.pillar2": "Assessment of the organisation's current data landscape, identifying gaps between existing capabilities and strategic ambitions across people, processes and technology.",
    "s1.pillar3": "Identification and prioritisation of value drivers and strategic data investment levers, balanced against the organisation's available resources, capacity and operational constraints.",
    "s1.pillar4": "Alignment of the data strategy with the organisation's existing technology landscape and architectural constraints, ensuring strategic decisions are grounded in operational and infrastructure reality.",
    "s1.pillar5": "Design of a phased transformation roadmap with clearly defined initiatives, milestone tracking and executive oversight mechanisms to ensure delivery accountability.",
    "s1.pillar6": "Assessment of the organisational readiness and change management considerations required to ensure the strategy is executable and sustainable beyond its initial definition.",
    "s1.value1.title": "A strategic data vision that holds",
    "s1.value1.body": "Ambitions, constraints and priorities translated into a direction the organisation can execute against, not just endorse.",
    "s1.value2.title": "Informed executive reporting",
    "s1.value2.body": "Senior leadership gains reliable, consistent visibility over data flows and operational activity across domains.",
    "s1.value3.title": "Regulatory and competitive readiness",
    "s1.value3.body": "A data strategy built to meet supervisory expectations in regulated sectors and to accelerate competitive positioning in others.",
    "s1.value4.title": "Decisions at the speed of the business",
