    "s4.value4.body": "A structured evaluation framework that assesses AI use cases against strategic priorities and quantified ROI before any deployment commitment is made.",
    "s4.value5.title": "Responsible and governed AI",
    "s4.value5.body": "An AI governance model covering the full lifecycle, aligned with GDPR, the EU AI Act and NIST AI RMF, ensuring adoption is auditable and supervisory-ready.",
    "s4.value6.title": "AI integrated into the data operating model",
    "s4.value6.body": "AI integration designed end-to-end, from data ingestion to analytical output, with full accountability embedded in the broader governance model.",

    //People Enablement & Data Literacy
    "s5.headline": "People Enablement & Data Literacy",
    "s5.sub1": "Organisations that treat data as a strategic asset do not just manage it better. They make better decisions, respond faster and build more resilient operating models. That shift does not happen through frameworks alone. It happens when people at every level, from the executive layer to the operational teams, genuinely understand what data represents for the organisation and take responsibility for it accordingly. This service drives that change in mindset, using governance frameworks, literacy programmes and organisational enablement as the tools that make it tangible and sustainable.",
    //"s5.sub2": "Through structured capability development, role-based literacy programmes, unified documentation and leadership alignment, organisations build the cultural and operational foundations needed to translate data ambition into consistent, informed and responsible decision-making.",
    // 2.1.5 People Enablement & Data Literacy
    "s5.pillar1": "Assessment of organisational data culture adoption barriers, identifying resistance patterns, capability gaps and the enablement mechanisms required to drive effective and sustained change.",
    "s5.pillar2": "Development of supporting documentation and transversal communication plans that build a common data language across the organisation, ensuring consistent understanding of data as a strategic asset at every level.",
    "s5.pillar3": "Design and delivery of structured training programmes by role and maturity level, combining conceptual grounding with practical application to ensure governance responsibilities and data practices are understood and exercised in context.",
    "s5.pillar4": "Tailored executive training on data integration within each business area's strategic priorities, ensuring senior leadership understands, champions and actively exploits data as a value asset in their decision-making.",
    "s5.pillar5": "Definition of incremental change management action plans to address identified adoption barriers, structured through pilots, day-in-the-life-of sessions and targeted workshops to ensure progressive and measurable deployment.",
    "s5.pillar6": "Establishment of adoption KPIs that provide ongoing visibility over cultural progress, measure the uptake of new ways of working and inform the evolution of enablement programmes over time.",
    "s5.value1.title": "Transformation that reaches the finish line",
    "s5.value1.body": "Resistance to new ways of working is the most common reason data programmes stall. This service identifies where that resistance occurs and puts in place the actions to overcome it.",
    "s5.value2.title": "Leadership that drives, not just endorses",
    "s5.value2.body": "Senior leaders are equipped to understand, champion and actively integrate data into their strategic decisions, not just approve it from a distance.",
    "s5.value3.title": "A common language for data",
    "s5.value3.body": "Documentation, communication and training build consistent understanding across the organisation, eliminating the ambiguity that slows adoption.",
    "s5.value4.title": "Change that is managed, not hoped for",
    "s5.value4.body": "Incremental action plans, pilots and targeted interventions ensure adoption progresses in a controlled and measurable way.",
    "s5.value5.title": "Roles that are lived, not assigned",
    "s5.value5.body": "Governance responsibilities and data practices become part of how people work, not an additional burden imposed from above.",
    "s5.value6.title": "Progress that can be measured",
    "s5.value6.body": "Adoption KPIs give the CDO visibility over cultural progress and the evidence needed to demonstrate transformation impact upwards.",

    // Values Declaration
    "values.headline": "A commitment to every engagement",
    "values.sub": "These are not corporate principles. They are the foundation of a way of working built on honesty, trust and the ambition to build relationships that last beyond any single engagement. Every conversation, every deliverable and every decision made on behalf of a client is guided by the same criteria. Because the quality of the work and the quality of the relationship are inseparable.",
    "values.v1.claim": "Honest counsel over comfortable advice",
    "values.v1.body": "The value of an outside perspective is its independence. Assessments and recommendations are grounded in genuine criteria, not in what is easiest to hear.",
    "values.v2.claim": "Commitment without conditions",
    "values.v2.body": "Every engagement is delivered with the same rigour, from the first conversation to the last deliverable.",
    "values.v3.claim": "Presence over process",
    "values.v3.body": "Proximity, discretion and genuine interest in the outcome are what turn a professional relationship into something of lasting value.",
    "values.v4.claim": "Clarity before complexity",
    "values.v4.body": "Complex work deserves clear communication. Whatever the technical depth of an engagement, the client always knows where things stand, what is being done and why.",


    // About Javier (4.1)
    "about.role": "Principal, Data Reinvention",
    "about.email": "Email",
    "about.linkedin": "LinkedIn",
    "about.label": "About Javier",
    "about.bio1": "I work at the intersection of data strategy, governance and organisational transformation. My practice is built around a single conviction: data only becomes a strategic asset when the structures, people and processes around it are designed to treat it as one. That conviction has shaped every engagement I have taken on, from defining enterprise data strategies for financial institutions to deploying governance frameworks that hold up under regulatory scrutiny and operational pressure.",
    "about.bio2": "My background spans top-tier advisory and technology consulting firms, where I have worked embedded within data domains of major financial institutions, leading governance transformations, designing data quality frameworks and driving the organisational change that makes those frameworks stick. I have conducted over 30 governance maturity workshops with business data domains, led end-to-end BCBS239-aligned framework deployments and contributed to the largest banking data migration programme in recent Spanish history. I have also designed and implemented enterprise governance platforms including Collibra, and developed AI use case evaluation frameworks with structured ROI assessment.",
    "about.bio3": "What defines my way of working is the ability to operate across the full vertical of a transformation. I am as comfortable presenting a governance roadmap to a CDO as I am sitting with a data engineering team to define validation controls. That range, between executive fluency and technical depth, is what Agora is built around.",

